  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "Tour 22: Frontend Core Mechanics & React Hooks",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "scripture-habit/src/components/groupchat/hooks/core/use-chat-sync-controller.ts",
      "description": "Welcome to **Tour 1: Frontend Core Mechanics**!\n\nWe start in **`useChatSyncController.ts`**. This React hook coordinates real-time unread count updates, visibility-aware read status updates, and handles infinite scrolling by reading older message documents or fallback JSON archive buckets.",
      "line": 15
    },
    {
      "file": "scripture-habit/src/components/groupchat/hooks/core/use-chat-sync-controller.ts",
      "description": "### Visibility-Aware Read Status Sync\n\nWhen a user shifts focus to the chat tab or the app returns to the foreground (`document.hasFocus()`), this effect detects new unread messages (`totalMsgs > userReadCount`) and triggers `updateReadStatus` to sync the read counters.",
      "line": 44
    },
    {
      "file": "scripture-habit/src/components/groupchat/hooks/core/use-chat-sync-controller.ts",
      "description": "### Infinite Scrolling & Fallback Message Buckets\n\nIf a user scrolls up to load historical chat transcripts:\n1. We fetch from the subcollection using `startAfter` (Cursor Pagination).\n2. If that subcollection is exhausted, we automatically sweep and unpack the compressed JSON `message_buckets` collection so users can scroll infinitely back into historical years.",
      "line": 74
    },
    {
      "file": "scripture-habit/src/components/groupchat/hooks/core/use-chat-data-engine.ts",
      "description": "Next, let's look at **`useChatDataEngine.ts`**.\n\nThis core engine coordinates active WebSockets via Firestore's `onSnapshot` to stream new incoming messages, group structural state updates, and live reactions.",
      "line": 13
    },
    {
      "file": "scripture-habit/src/components/groupchat/hooks/core/use-chat-data-engine.ts",
      "description": "### Real-Time Live Message Stream via Previews (`messages_latest/latest`)\n\nInstead of querying a heavy collection directly, we open a single `onSnapshot` listener on the aggregated `messages_latest/latest` document. This dramatically minimizes Firestore reads and instantly merges real-time incoming messages with local optimistic updates (prefixed with `temp-`).",
      "line": 154
    },
    {
      "file": "scripture-habit/src/components/dashboard/hooks/use-dashboard-actions.ts",
      "description": "Finally, we explore **`useDashboardActions.ts`**.\n\nThis acts as the bridge connecting study activities, level transitions, and user profile metrics directly to Firestore database writes.",
      "line": 17
    }
  ]
}